relations.

* `tabT`, `parT`: the generation tree of `g* ⊗ g*` (784 tables) from `δ₂₇⊗δ₂₇` by the pair operators
  `S_x`, `A_x`: level 0 (300 tables, `V(2θ)`), level 1 (378, `Λ²`), level 2 (106, complement of
  `V(2θ)` in `Sym²`); depth `≤ 4`.
* `UT`, `UcertT`: the tables `U_r` (dual to the relations under `ψ`, scaled by 768) as level-2
  combinations.
* `antiCT`, `symCT`: the certificates for `8 (e_c⊗e_d - e_d⊗e_c)` (level ≤ 1) and
  `384 (e_c⊗e_d + e_d⊗e_c) - Σ_r ψ_r(c,d) U_r` (level 0).

The Boolean checks are defined here and evaluated in `DeligneDivisorD4Checks` (split into small
kernel checks).
-/

